        "review": {
          "approved": false,
          "summary": "EvidenceStorage implementation has a critical bug: storeEvidence is async but tests call it synchronously without await, causing unhandled promise rejections and false test passes. Duplicate detection hashes the full evidence object including its own hash field, so re-storing identical content with a different timestamp is not detected as duplicate content. Test setup creates storage before deleting the file, leaving stale data. Missing timestamp check occurs after duplicate check, so duplicate-with-missing-timestamp is misreported. No provenance fields (retrieval time, parser version, uncertainty) per Issue requirements. No append-only correction behavior test.",
          "needs_gpt_decision": true,
          "reason": "Code correctness defects and missing required provenance fields cannot be cleared by reviewer opinion; GPT decision required.",
